target
# Nested Cargo target dirs (e.g. plugins/reference-materializer/target) — the
# top-level `target` glob only matches at the context root, so without this a
# locally-built plug-in ships its whole target dir in the build context.
**/target
# ⚠ ...but NOT inside `vendor/`. `**/target` is a NAME match, so it also
# excludes `vendor/cc/src/target/` — a legitimate SOURCE module of the vendored
# `cc` crate, not a build directory. The result is a vendor tree that looks
# complete and fails at `cargo chef cook` with
# "failed to open /app/vendor/cc/src/target/llvm.rs", which reads like a
# corrupt vendor rather than an ignore rule. Re-include vendored sources
# explicitly; vendored crates ship no build artifacts, so nothing is regained
# by excluding them.
!vendor/**
.git
.github
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
tmp
